        'Copying moves income and expenses only, never savings. Savings is a recorded balance, so a copy made the month claim savings you never entered — the Year tab showed "0 kr" instead of "not recorded". That applied to "Next month" too, which is now fixed',
        'If the month already has amounts you get a confirmation first, and an empty previous month is never pulled',
        'The "Trend" chart type is gone from the Custom layout. It always drew bars despite showing as selected. Existing blocks using it now display as Bars and keep their name, rows, colors, size and position',
        'Backup now refuses a file holding chart settings the app cannot display, instead of importing them and leaving the settings panel blank',
        'New: the Custom layout has a year overview. Switch between 📋 Budget and 📅 Year at the top — the whole year with in, out, saved and left, plus totals. Until now you could only ever see one month, because Custom hides the tab bar',
        'In the year overview a month you never filled in shows "–", not 0 kr. Saved is summed across the year, because Custom stores what you set aside each month',
        'New: duplicate a block with ⧉ in edit mode. The copy keeps the same rows, colors and chart settings and lands right after the original — but without amounts, so you fill it in fresh',
        'New: ready-made blocks in "Add block" — Housing, Food, Transport and Savings, with the right type and pre-named rows. They follow a language switch like every other built-in name',
        'New: a line under the summary cards that says something about the month instead of only showing figures — your largest expense, how much you set aside, or a deficit. If a goal is within reach or your savings have grown several months running, it says that instead',
        'New: a row can fall due quarterly or yearly. Type the amount you actually pay — 4,800 kr for the insurance — and mark the row "Yearly". The budget counts 400 kr a month instead of making January look like a disaster. Touch nothing and everything stays monthly as before',
        'New: a pay-period line under the month. Set the day your period starts and the app writes "25 Dec – 24 Jan" under every month. Prefer your own words for one month? Click the text and type — clear the field to go back to automatic. It is only a label: no amounts change',
        'Changed: "Yearly" no longer divides the amount by twelve. An annual subscription is charged in full in the month you pay it, so the budget matches your account that month. New option: One-off',
        'Rows that do not recur monthly are no longer carried along when you copy the budget forward — otherwise February would show a charge that never happens. You add them back when they fall due',
        'Fixed: copying no longer overwrites a month without asking. The prompt names the month and the source, and "All remaining" counts how many are affected first. Cancel and nothing is written',
        'Fixed: the Savings tab offered a period control, which made one account show 12,000 kr and 1,000 kr at once. A balance is what you have, not something that gets charged',
        'Fixed: the Custom year overview changed history when you edited today\'s layout. Each month now records its own structure, so September stands even if you delete the block in October',
        'Fixed: the Custom year view was squeezed into a narrow column, a pay period starting on the 1st showed the previous month, and a corrupt period marking could empty a total',
        'Fixed: "Pull from last month" could empty a finished budget. A month holding only savings or just a period label counted as a budget to pull from — it now needs real budget content, and otherwise nothing happens',
        'Custom months recorded before the app started saving their structure are given it retroactively. Without it, editing today\'s layout reclassified older months. No amounts are touched',
        'Deleting a single row in Custom now asks first, exactly as deleting a whole block did — and the warning counts the month you are standing in as well',
        'The warning explains what actually happens: the rows leave the monthly budget but the amounts stay counted in the year overview, so the two views show different figures',
        '"Clear amounts" now also removes the structure notes that belonged to those amounts, instead of leaving them behind with nothing to describe',
        'Fixed: the menu could not be scrolled on desktop. In a short window its lower half fell outside the screen, and because the header is pinned, scrolling the page did not help — Import data and the whole danger zone were simply unreachable. The menu now stays inside the window and the list scrolls',
        'Fixed: a row that is not monthly stated its period twice — "One-off" in the picker and "one-off cost" beside it — and the picker was clipped mid-word. The period is named in one place now, and the whole word fits',
        'Fixed: with the app open in two tabs, one could silently overwrite the other. Raise the salary in one tab and change the rent in the other, and only the rent survived — with no warning. Tabs now keep up with each other, so both edits stand',
        'Fixed: in the Custom layout the menu offered Copy budget and Reset month — but they acted on the Classic budget, data you were not looking at, and still reported success. They now appear only in Classic and Combined, where they belong',
        'Fixed: a damaged language or currency setting left the app completely blank at start, with no menu left to change it back. Both are now checked, at startup and on import — a backup carrying an unknown language is refused instead of first replacing your budget',
        'New: if the browser refuses to save — full storage, or storage switched off — the app says so instead of letting the change look saved. The change stays on screen, and from there you can retry or export your data',
        'Fixed: in Expense distribution the percentage was measured against income while the circle was drawn from expenses. A lone expense filled the whole circle and was still labelled 45 %. Both are now a share of expenses',
        'Fixed: on mobile the summary amounts were cut off — 30 000,50 kr became 30 000,5… The cards now sit two across with Left below, so ordinary amounts with decimals are fully visible even on a 320 px screen',
        'Fixed: the year chart compared different kinds of number. Income and expenses are flows, the savings figure is a balance — but all three were drawn as equal bars, so a 48 000 kr pot became the tallest bar of the year every month and flattened the figures the chart is named after. The balance is now a line on its own axis on the right',
        'Fixed: a month you never filled in showed as 0 kr in the year overview — a month with no earnings and no spending. It now shows –, exactly as the savings column already did. A month you built and left at zero still counts as a real zero',
        'Fixed: Goal progress showed 0 % before you had created any goal — a score in a game you had not started. It now shows – with an explanation, like the cards beside it',
        'Changed: between 640 and 900 px the summary cards stacked one per row, so a half-width window spent more height on three numbers than a phone does. They now sit three across and the charts are visible without scrolling',
